'''Slayers''' are {{Skl|Combat}}-oriented missions that involve killing a specific type of mob and gaining {{Skl|Combat|XP}}, culminating with defeating a {{Mcat|Slayer Boss}}.

== Overview ==
'''Slayer Quests''' can be started for a {{c}} fee by talking to {{NPCSprite|Maddox the Slayer}} under the {{Zone|Tavern}} at {{Coordinates|-83.5|68|-129.5}}, or remotely using a {{Item|Maddox Batphone}} or {{Item|Abiphone}}.

Only {{Green|1}} '''Slayer Quest''' can be active at a time.

Once a '''Slayer Quest''' is started, the specified amount of {{Skl|Combat|XP}} must be earned from killing the Slayer's respective mob:
*This amount of {{Skl|combat|XP}} increases with the tier of the '''Slayer Quest''', but so does the {{c}} fee.
*{{SlayerTier|III}}+ '''Slayer Quests''' may also spawn {{Mcat|Slayer Miniboss}}, which are stronger and grant significantly more {{Skl|Combat|XP}}. 
*{{SlayerTier|V}} {{Mcat|Slayer Bosses}} often have different names and express unique traits. 

Defeating a {{Mcat|Slayer Boss}}  will complete the '''Slayer Quest''': the player can then claim {{LightPurple|Slayer XP}}, which increases the player's '''Slayer level''' for its corresponding Slayer. 
*'''Slayer Levels''' unlock crafting recipes and permanent stat boosts, with some granting unique perks.
Defeating a {{Mcat|Slayer Boss}}  will also award the following:
* {{Aqua|'''Token'''}} drops: they are {{Odds|guaranteed}}, drop in varying numbers and are used in lots of recipes unlocked from its corresponding slayer. 
**{{aqua|Token}} drops have a compacted form that are used in more recipes, crafted using another commodity: for example, {{Item|Tarantula Silk}} is crafted using {{Item|Tarantula Web}}s and {{Item|Enchanted Flint}}.
**Most {{SlayerTier|V}} variants of each {{Mcat|Slayer Boss}} have a chance to drop the upgraded form of their respective {{aqua|Token}} drop. For example, the {{MobSprite|Atoned Horror}} has a chance to drop {{Item|Revenant Viscera}}s.
* And possibly, rare and powerful items…

