== RNG Meter ==

{{Main|RNG Meter}}

The '''RNG Meter''' is unlocked for each individual {{Mcat|Slayer Boss}} type upon slaying their respective {{SlayerTier|3}} {{Mcat|Slayer Boss}}. {{Pink|Slayer XP}} gained from killing {{Stier|3}}, {{Stier|4}}, and {{Stier|5}} {{Mcat|Slayer Bosses}} will increment their corresponding [[Pity and RNG Meters#Slayer|{{Pink|RNG Meter}}]]. Players can select a drop in the {{Pink|RNG Meter}}, increasing the chances of that item dropping: upon filling the meter, the player is guaranteed to drop their selected item on the {{Mcat|Slayer Boss}} of an eligible tier.
<!--{{:RNG Meter/Slayer}}-->

== Trivia ==
* {{Mcat|Slayer Minibosses}} despawn after not being interacted with after {{More Info Needed}}.
* In order to get a {{coll|Slayer|9}} from scratch and without external bonuses nor fails, it would take:
** {{Green|2000}} {{SlayerTier|IV}}, costing {{c|100m}};
** or {{Green|200}} {{SlayerTier|IV}} and {{Green|600}} {{SlayerTier|V}}, costing {{c|70m}}.
* Contributing {{Green|24}} times to the [[City_Projects#Bartender's_Brewery|Bartender's Brewery]] [[City Project]] granted a {{Green|5%}} discount on [[Slayers]], overriding the {{Green|4%}} discount perk gained from reaching LVL {{green|7}} on the first {{green|3}} [[Slayers]].
* Should a server reboots when a player has a [[Slayer]] {{Boss}} summoned, it will despawn and progress towards the '''Slayer Quest''' will be set to the maximum amount of {{Skl|Combat|XP}}. The next mob killed will immediately spawn it again, providede that the mob was eligible to contribute to the '''Slayer Quest''' progress.
* When [[Enderman Slayer]] was released, all players lost access to [[Auto-Slayer]] due to not having {{collection|Enderman Slayer|6}}. However, players who had it on before the update would be able to use it, and would not be able to disable it.
* Due to {{stat|Magic Find}} only affecting the drops under a {{green|5%}} chance, getting higher {{stat|mf}} will not push the drop chance to {{green|100%}}. Instead:
** For any item affected by {{stat|mf}}: <math>\lim_{{\color{Aqua}\text{MF}} \to +\infty}{\color{JungleGreen}\text{Percent Drop Chance}} = \frac{{\color{JungleGreen}\text{New Weight}_1}}{\displaystyle\sum _{{\color{Aqua}\text{MF}}\text{-affected}}{\color{JungleGreen}\text{New Weights}_1}}</math>
** For any other non-{{Odds|Guaranteed}} item:  <math>\lim_{{\color{Aqua}\text{MF}} \to +\infty}{\color{JungleGreen}\text{Percent Drop Chance}} = 0</math>.

